  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved safety and health and workplace compliance in industrial zones</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the declaration of a safe and healthy working environment as a fundamental principle and right at work at the 110th session of the ILC, the two fundamental Conventions are ILO Conventions C155 on Occupational Safety and Health, 1981, and C187 on the Promotional Framework for Occupational Safety and Health, 2006. In line with this declaration, the ILO adopted a new occupational safety and health strategy to assist its constituents in adopting and implementing the two fundamental ILO Conventions.
Despite Egypt&apos;s efforts to improve working conditions and protect workers, the frequency and severity of occupational accidents have a negative impact on the economy, reducing the productivity of industries and consequently affecting the level of international exports. The ILO is supporting several OSH initiatives in Egypt to help the country prepare for the ratification of the two OSH Conventions and the establishment of its first OSH policy: a gap analysis for the ratification of Conventions C155 and C187, an OSH profile and training for labour inspectors to improve compliance. 
The ILO is also supporting Egypt in the progressive realisation of decent work for all workers, in line with SDG 8, by extending protection to all workers in all sectors of activity.</narrative>
  </description>
